# react-geek-form Patterns

## Overview

This project uses `react-geek-form` via a custom `createForm` utility that wraps `createInstance` with pre-configured form components from `@repo/multiverse-ui`.

## Core Setup

### createForm Utility

The `createForm` utility is defined in `packages/utilities/src/createForm.ts` and wraps `createInstance` from `react-geek-form`:

```tsx
import { createForm } from "@repo/utilities";

const { forwardFormContext, TextInput, SelectInput, CheckBoxGroup } = createForm({
  zodSchema: entityFormSchema,
});
```

**Always import `createForm` from `@repo/utilities`, never directly from `react-geek-form`.**

## Form Component Creation

### Basic Pattern

```tsx
import { createForm } from "@repo/utilities";
import { entityFormSchema } from "../schemas";

const { forwardFormContext, TextInput, SelectInput } = createForm({
  zodSchema: entityFormSchema,
});

const EntityFormModal = forwardFormContext(
  ({ onClose, onSubmit, initialValues, isLoading }, ctx) => {
    // Form implementation
  }
);
```

### Available Form Components

From `createForm`, you get access to:
- `TextInput` - Text input with label and validation
- `PasswordInput` - Password input with label
- `NumberInput` - Numeric input with formatting
- `TextArea` - Multi-line text input
- `SelectInput` - Dropdown select (supports `type="multiple"` for arrays)
- `CheckBoxGroup` - Checkbox group for multiple selection
- `RadioGroup` - Radio button group for exclusive selection
- `DatePicker` - Date selection
- `DropzoneField` - File upload with drag & drop
- `Switch` - Toggle switch for boolean values
- `MaskInput` - Masked input (e.g., phone numbers)
- `PinInput` - PIN code input
- `QuantityInput` - Quantity selector with increment/decrement
- `YearPicker` - Year selection
- `LogoInput` - Logo upload input

### Form Context Methods

The `ctx` parameter from `forwardFormContext` provides:

#### `ctx.useSetDefaultValues(values)`
Set default/initial values for the form. Use conditionally for edit forms:

```tsx
if (initialValues) {
  ctx.useSetDefaultValues({
    email: initialValues.email,
    first_name: initialValues.first_name,
    role_ids: initialValues.roles.map((role) => role.id),
  });
}
```

#### `ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit, onError?)`
Handle form submission with validation:

```tsx
<form onSubmit={ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit, (errors) => {
  console.log(errors);
})}>
```

#### `ctx.setZodSchema(schema)`
Dynamically change the form schema (useful for conditional validation):

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (initialValues) {
    ctx.setZodSchema(userFormSchema.omit({ password: true }));
  }
}, [ctx, initialValues]);
```

#### `ctx.setValue(name, value)`
Programmatically set field values:

```tsx
ctx.setValue("name", "New Value");
ctx.setValue("member_price", [{ price: 0, tier_id: undefined }]);
```

#### `useWatch({ name: ["field1", "field2"] })`
Watch specific fields for changes:

```tsx
const { forwardFormContext, useWatch } = createForm({ zodSchema });

const [category_id] = useWatch({ name: ["category_id"] });
```

#### `useFieldArray({ name: "fieldName" })`
Manage dynamic arrays of fields:

```tsx
const { forwardFormContext, useFieldArray } = createForm({ zodSchema });

const { fields, append, remove } = useFieldArray({ name: "items" });

// Use in JSX
{fields.map((field, index) => (
  <Stack key={field.id} horizontal>
    <TextInput name={`items.${index}.name`} />
    <Button onClick={() => remove(index)}>Remove</Button>
  </Stack>
))}
```

## Form Implementation Patterns

### Modal Form Pattern

```tsx
const EntityFormModal = forwardFormContext(
  ({ onClose, onSubmit, initialValues, isLoading }, ctx) => {
    // Set default values for edit mode
    if (initialValues) {
      ctx.useSetDefaultValues({
        ...initialValues,
        // Transform nested data if needed
        role_ids: initialValues.roles.map((role) => role.id),
      });
    }

    return (
      <Modal onClose={onClose} title={initialValues ? "Edit" : "Create"}>
        <form onSubmit={ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
          <Stack gap={16}>
            <TextInput name="name" label="Name" />
            <SelectInput
              name="status"
              label="Status"
              options={[
                { label: "Active", value: "ACTIVE" },
                { label: "Inactive", value: "INACTIVE" },
              ]}
            />
            
            <Stack horizontal gap={12} justify="end" className="mt-mds-24">
              <Button intent="default" onClick={onClose} loading={isLoading}>
                Cancel
              </Button>
              <Button type="submit" intent="primary" loading={isLoading}>
                {initialValues ? "Save Changes" : "Create"}
              </Button>
            </Stack>
          </Stack>
        </form>
      </Modal>
    );
  }
);
```

### Page Form Pattern

```tsx
const AddEntity = forwardFormContext((_, ctx) => {
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  
  // Set default values
  ctx.useSetDefaultValues({
    items: [{ name: "", quantity: 1 }],
  });

  const { fields, append, remove } = useFieldArray({ name: "items" });

  return (
    <>
      <Breadcrumb label="Add Entity" />
      <PageWrapper>
        <form onSubmit={ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
          {/* Form fields */}
        </form>
      </PageWrapper>
    </>
  );
});
```

## Field Types and Usage

### TextInput
```tsx
<TextInput
  name="email"
  label="Email"
  type="email"
  placeholder="Enter email"
  disabled={!!initialValues} // Disable in edit mode
/>
```

### SelectInput (Single)
```tsx
<SelectInput
  name="status"
  label="Status"
  placeholder="Select status"
  options={[
    { label: "Active", value: "ACTIVE" },
    { label: "Inactive", value: "INACTIVE" },
  ]}
/>
```

### SelectInput (Multiple)
```tsx
<SelectInput
  name="role_ids"
  label="Select Roles"
  type="multiple"
  options={roleList?.map((role) => ({
    label: role.name,
    value: role.id,
  })) ?? []}
/>
```

### CheckBoxGroup
```tsx
<CheckBoxGroup
  name="permissionIds"
  label="Select Permissions"
  className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4"
>
  {permissionList?.map((permission) => (
    <CheckBoxGroup.Item
      key={permission.id}
      value={permission.id}
      label={permission.name}
      description={permission.description}
    />
  )) ?? []}
</CheckBoxGroup>
```

**Note:** CheckBoxGroup values are transformed. If your schema expects `z.array(z.number())`, the form library handles the transformation automatically.

### DropzoneField
```tsx
<DropzoneField
  name="img_url"
  label="Upload Image"
  api={api}
  imageOnly={true}
/>
```

### NumberInput
```tsx
<NumberInput
  name="amount"
  label="Amount"
  placeholder="Enter amount"
  min={0}
  max={10000}
/>
```

### TextArea
```tsx
<TextArea
  name="description"
  label="Description"
  placeholder="Enter description"
  rows={4}
/>
```

## Schema Patterns

### Basic Form Schema
```tsx
export const entityFormSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1, "Name is required").max(50),
  email: z.string().email("Invalid email"),
  role_ids: z.array(z.number()).min(1, "At least one role is required"),
});
```

### Conditional Schema Updates
For forms that change validation based on mode (create vs edit):

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (initialValues) {
    ctx.setZodSchema(entityFormSchema.omit({ password: true }));
  } else {
    ctx.setZodSchema(entityFormSchema);
  }
}, [ctx, initialValues]);
```

## Error Handling

### 422 Form Error Handling

Use `use422FormErrorSetter` for API validation errors:

```tsx
import { use422FormErrorSetter } from "@repo/hooks";

const EntityFormModal = forwardFormContext(({ onClose, onSubmit }, ctx) => {
  const { onError, setConfig } = use422FormErrorSetter();
  
  // Pass form context methods
  useEffect(() => {
    setConfig({
      watch: ctx.watch,
      setError: ctx.setError,
      getValues: ctx.getValues,
      clearErrors: ctx.clearErrors,
    });
  }, [ctx, setConfig]);

  return (
    <form onSubmit={ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      {/* Form fields */}
    </form>
  );
});
```

Or pass context directly:

```tsx
const { onError } = use422FormErrorSetter(ctx);
```

Then use in mutation:

```tsx
createEntity(payload, {
  onSuccess: () => {
    close();
    invalidateEntityListQuery();
  },
  onError, // Handles 422 validation errors
});
```

## Best Practices

1. **Always use `createForm` from `@repo/utilities`** - Never import directly from `react-geek-form`

2. **Destructure only needed components** - Only destructure what you use:
   ```tsx
   const { forwardFormContext, TextInput, SelectInput } = createForm({
     zodSchema: entityFormSchema,
   });
   ```

3. **Use conditional default values** - Set defaults only when needed:
   ```tsx
   if (initialValues) {
     ctx.useSetDefaultValues({ ...initialValues });
   }
   ```

4. **Transform nested data** - Map nested objects to form-compatible structures:
   ```tsx
   ctx.useSetDefaultValues({
     role_ids: initialValues.roles.map((role) => role.id),
   });
   ```

5. **Handle password fields** - Omit password from edit forms:
   ```tsx
   {!initialValues && <PasswordInput name="password" label="Password" />}
   ```

6. **Use proper field names** - Field names must match schema keys exactly

7. **Type form props** - Use inferred types from schema:
   ```tsx
   type EntityForm = z.infer<typeof entityFormSchema>;
   
   onSubmit: (payload: EntityForm) => void;
   ```

8. **Handle loading states** - Pass `isLoading` to buttons:
   ```tsx
   <Button type="submit" loading={isLoading}>Submit</Button>
   ```

## Common Patterns

### Create/Update Modal Hook Pattern

```tsx
const useEntityUpdateCreation = () => {
  const { mutate: createEntity, isPending: isCreating } = useCreateEntityMutation();
  const { mutate: updateEntity, isPending: isUpdating } = useUpdateEntityMutation();
  const createOverlay = useCreateOverlay({ isCreating, isUpdating });

  const openCreateEntityModal = useCallback(() => {
    createOverlay({
      component: ({ close, state: { isCreating } }) => (
        <EntityFormModal
          onClose={close}
          onSubmit={(payload) =>
            createEntity(payload, {
              onSuccess: () => {
                close();
                invalidateEntityListQuery();
              },
            })
          }
          isLoading={isCreating}
        />
      ),
    });
  }, [createOverlay, createEntity]);

  const openUpdateEntityModal = useCallback(
    (initialValues: Entity) => {
      createOverlay({
        component: ({ close, state: { isUpdating } }) => (
          <EntityFormModal
            onClose={close}
            initialValues={initialValues}
            onSubmit={(payload) =>
              updateEntity(
                { id: initialValues.id, payload },
                {
                  onSuccess: () => {
                    close();
                    invalidateEntityListQuery();
                  },
                }
              )
            }
            isLoading={isUpdating}
          />
        ),
      });
    },
    [createOverlay, updateEntity]
  );

  return { openCreateEntityModal, openUpdateEntityModal };
};
```
